WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:03.496
- Humans can experience
over 10 million colors.

00:00:03.496 --> 00:00:04.975
It's rather amazing

00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:07.308
but not to the mantis shrimp.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:12.507
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:00:12.507 --> 00:00:14.209
This is a mantis shrimp.

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:17.149
Mantis shrimp have 16 color
receptors in their eyes,

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:20.842
the most of any animal on our planet.

00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:22.170
Now what does this mean?

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.189
Now think about the world you live in.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:28.412
You're experiencing all this
with three optical receptors.

00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:31.246
Because the mantis shrimp
has so many more than us,

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:35.011
their light detecting ability
is astronomically better

00:00:35.011 --> 00:00:37.705
and this can help them spot pray quicker,

00:00:37.705 --> 00:00:40.551
making it an extraordinary hunter.

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:42.851
It's only about four inches long

00:00:42.851 --> 00:00:46.518
but can strike with the
force of 335 pounds.

00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:48.850
- Wow.

00:00:50.811 --> 00:00:53.501
- It takes nine pounds to break a nose,

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.699
25 to break a small bone

00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:59.377
and 400 to break through
a block of cement.

00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:01.261
The movement of the mantis shrimp claw

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:05.607
is one of the fastest
for any animal on earth.

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:10.383
They've even been know to
break through aquarium tanks.

00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:11.300
Remarkable.

